 ;; missed: missed; clang-extra: extra, or line 0; clang-elsewhere: stopped), the oracle tier's comparison
 {:id :own-diag
  :title "neither judge meets the file's dg-error lines: Arbace's own front end's diagnostics not ported"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "clang's record (the row's reason: its errors against the directives) and Arbace's own front end's record (test/cpp/check-dg-own-linux-amd64.edn: the native parser's and arbace.cpp.sema's errors, CX12) both fail the file, which asks standard C++ (the dialects are :gcc-dialect's, GCC's own rules :gcc-own-rules'): a Sema check (lookup, conversions, overloads, constant evaluation, templates, access) or a parser diagnostic the own front end does not give yet, or its recovery's errors on other lines: CX12's gap (queue 336: each file's Sema rule, its group and clauses, in test/cpp/own-diag-review.edn, the plan of CX12's next slices)"
  :decided "CP398 (a) (the user, 2026-11-17): before, CX9's clang-pedantic, clang-accepts, clang-other-lines, clang-fewer-errors, clang-extra and clang-elsewhere, by design under CP2 (a)"
  :match [#"^fail (extra|both): .*\[-Werror,-W" #"^fail missed: accepted; " #"^fail both: " #"^fail missed: missed " #"^fail extra: " #"^fail missed: line 0 expects" #"^fail stopped: "]}
 {:id :dg-unsupported
  :title "DejaGnu's UNSUPPORTED: a directive's selector is false on this target, or the directory's driver is not modelled"
  :kind :na
  :why "a dg-do, dg-skip-if or dg-require selector false on x86-64 Linux with g++ 15.2 at the standards the run takes (ia32, mingw, darwin, aarch64, ! c++11 ...), or a directory whose .exp driver builds something first (pch, plugin, debug's -g levels, ecos): not a test here, as C's class of the same name (CS195 (a)); not applicable since CP260 (a): a test DejaGnu does not run here has no verdict to pass, so it is outside both denominators"
  :decided "CS195 (a) for C; cppi-check (2026-11-05) for C++, CX9's verdict unsupported; :na by CP260 (a) (the user, 2026-11-08)"
  :match [#"^unsupported"]}
 {:id :read-refused
  :title "repr/cpp's converter refuses a unit the oracle accepts"
  :kind :gap
  :why "a construct the converter has no form for in a macro (CP79 (b)'s refusals) or a gap it reports (:cpp/gap): the read level's open cases (CX4-CX5's classes, test/repr/cpp/roundtrip-known.edn)"
  :decided "CX9; CX5"
  :match [#"^fail refused: "]}
 {:id :oracle-crash
